hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer questions  from one of my foreign readers swan 55  who was asking about Twitter and how to  use it to market your business in your  products so a quick story about me on  Twitter when I first saw the service I  thought it was pointless and I wouldn't  use it I saw you know people talking  about their cats and where they're  getting lunch and I didn't really care  about that but then I did a quick search  for my name and found the people we're  talking about me on Twitter and they  were sharing content for my articles and  talking about what I was up to on  Twitter and I wasn't part of the  conversation so that's what got me to  join and at first I was just listening  to see what people were saying and  recognizing champions and thinking  people and then I started to get more  involved instead of posting and started  to becoming an expert in thought leader  and I found a lot of value from using  Twitter for my business so I'm going to  share with you five ways that you can  use Twitter to market your products and  hopefully can use some of them to two  great business so the first one is you  use twitter to sell and i haven't had  experience really with this and i don't  really believe in using this method but  i wanted to put it up there because  that's what most people think at the  start and this method is basically  you're you're pushing links out and  you're just promoting your product out  there you know however many times a day  you want to you want to put out there  sometimes of doing hundreds of posts  every day with affiliate links or links  to your own products and you know you're  hoping somebody's doing a search and  you're coming up right away because you  posted it so recently and they go on the  land on your page and sign of your  newsletter or your buy your product I  don't have a lot of experience with that  I don't know how much it works I know  when I see those I never click on the  links and I don't go and buy those  products but if people are doing it  there's got to be some money some money  in it so that's something you can  explore but I don't recommend it I  prefer using as Twitter as a way to  build relationships people and from  there you can generate some business so  the next one is become an expert  and here what you're doing is you're  trying to establish yourself as a  thought leader for whatever industry  you're in so for me I talk about  entrepreneurship and I'm seen as an  expert in entrepreneurship and people  follow me on Twitter to hear what I have  to say about entrepreneurship and  articles i'm reading and famous quotes  that inspire me and new content we're  coming up with and that's a reason to  follow me on twitter and then from there  people want to do business with me  because people want to do business with  the leaders in the experts in the  industry so you can use twitter to  establish yourself as an expert in  whatever industry you're in so you  didn't mention what you were selling  their what products you were trying to  market but whatever it is I tried to set  up a schedule of tweets to go out to  showcase how you're the most  knowledgeable person in the world about  whatever product it is that you're  selling and how useful it can be for  people and then from there people become  interested they look at your profile  they look at your website and they want  to come up and buy your products or  services so it's a little bit of a  longer strategy to establish out  expertise but you're attracting higher  quality clients who will likely buy more  from you stay longer firmer friends get  tuned to the media on and on and on and  on so definitely worth it in my opinion  the third way you can use it is the  prospect and what you're doing here is  you basically look for keywords that  people are typing in who are potential  customers for you and you can do it by  location as well so if you have a  physical location you can geosearch so  you can say within you know 20  kilometers or 20 miles of whatever  location or just in whatever city or  whatever country and you're looking for  people who are tweeting about certain  keywords and then you can respond to  them so an example if you had a coffee  shop you could you know search for the  word coffee and see what people are  tweeting and if somebody is you know  within 10 miles or 10 kilometers of your  location and they're saying I really  need a coffee then it's an opportunity  for you to connect with them and  introduce yourself and so start building  relationship with them for a while I was  even tracking the keywords entrepreneur  and help or business and help and people  were asking questions online on Twitter  and I would just start responding to  people and start building relationships  with people  there was necessarily business model  it's just something that I impassioned  about and really enjoy doing and I now  haven't done it because I get so many  questions coming at me that making these  videos takes up a lot of time and I  don't really have the time to do that  anymore but it was a great way to start  making some important connections at the  beginning and if I had something to sell  on my site if I answered their question  really helped them out they're going to  go to my Twitter bio look at my link and  click on my website and if I had a  product some of them would buy it so  it's a great way to start introducing  yourself to people who are potential  customers for you number four is connect  and what you can do here is you try to  introduce yourself to people who could  have a meaningful impact on your  business so connectors media potential  partners influencers people who could  refer business to you or say good things  about you that would lead to business  coming into your company and you can use  twitter is a great way to be able to  connect with them so you can introduce  yourself to them you can tweet out some  of the messages that they're writing you  can comment on some of their tweets so  basically if people are doing on an  ongoing basis and I notice it online to  people who often respond to my tweets  are retweeting what I'm writing I  noticed some and if it happens enough  then i'll usually click on their site  and i've become curious and what they're  doing so if you do it enough times if  you've kind of identified the people who  you want to go after and introduce  yourself to that could be a great way to  get on their radar screen and prompt  some kind of dialogue and introduction  to be able to then hopefully do some  business together longer term i also use  twitter when I'm first connecting with  people who are meeting locally so if  somebody is in Toronto and I've  scheduled a meeting with them I'll  quickly see if they have a Twitter  account or not to then be able to  connect with them and learn a little bit  about them before I end up going and  meeting with them so quick example is  meeting with a potential client downtown  here in Toronto and I researched the  person's Twitter account and found out  that she really liked a certain bakery  that was close to her office so I my way  down I stopped off at the breaker II  picked up some treats and brought them  to the meeting and so it's her favorite  bakery you know  lots of treats so the meeting started  off on a great foot and went well from  there on as well so it's a great way to  kind of learn a little bit about the  people the research into them before you  meet them and allows you to kind of gear  your conversation towards things that  maybe you have in common that you can  kind of get in there faster and make  that connection a little bit more easy  so that's number four and then the last  one that I would use it to do is update  your customers so here people will post  news updates or different updates about  what's going on at the business and it's  a great way for customers to kind of  keep track of what you're up to what  you're doing now this only works if you  have customers who actually care about  your business right if you're doing the  first one and all you're doing is  selling you're not gonna have people who  are actually following you and care  about your updates so you have to make  sure that you have a loyal fan base and  from there you can use the updates to  kind of keep in touch with them one  thing that will do with on the update  side at least is we'll post information  about what's going on in our website but  then we'll also try to follow some of  our customers and look for ways to  recognize them so what we try to do is  send a brownie every week to somebody on  our list and we look for ways on Twitter  people to do that so an example one of  our authors or customers was on Twitter  and posted that she couldn't go to work  and she had to work from starbucks  because the air conditioning on a very  hot summer day was broken at her office  she was working from starbucks so we saw  that we you know responded by Twitter  and then we sent her a brownie in the  mail to say you know I hope the air  conditioning gets fixed soon and here's  some sweet treats to keep it going while  you're working out of starbucks and she  was really grateful and the fact that  people were connecting on Twitter and  that we saw that post and cared about  her enough to respond that helps us  stand out and it's easier to win these  customers over for life and doesn't take  a lot of work and it's also fun to do so  those are some of the ways that we've  used it and hopefully through those  stories is something you can do for your  business as well if you guys liked the  video I love to hear comments if you  want to leave one under the video and  always love seeing those thumbs ups if  you can leave one under the video it  helps me know that you guys like these  and I'll keep making more for you  so thank you look forward to hearing  from you and we'll see you on the next  episode  you
 

